{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_development_development_guide", "label": "Development guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L1-L15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing needs a GPU, an API key, or network access; the two CI gates (ruff check, backlog.py check) are the same commands a contributor runs locally."}, {"id": "docs_development_testing_conventions", "label": "Testing conventions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L17-L42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_development_network_free_tests", "label": "Network-free test suite", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L19-L21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every external call is mocked so pytest passes offline; real vendor payloads are checked in as fixtures instead, refreshed by record_fixtures.py."}, {"id": "docs_development_behaviour_named_tests", "label": "Behaviour-named tests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L22-L24", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The name states the property being asserted, so a failure report reads as a claim that stopped holding."}, {"id": "docs_development_test_first_for_bug_fixes", "label": "Test-first for bug fixes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L26-L29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not ceremony: writing failure-path tests for the CLI found two real defects success-path tests could not have, because 18 of those tests asserted exit_code == 0 and therefore tested nothing about failure."}, {"id": "docs_development_assert_the_invariant", "label": "Assert the invariant, not the output", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L31-L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A test pinned to a number breaks on every legitimate change and catches nothing structural."}, {"id": "docs_development_never_weaken_a_test", "label": "Never weaken a test to make it pass", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L36-L38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a test starts failing, the default assumption is that the code broke. A test that cannot fail is worse than no test."}, {"id": "docs_development_research_scripts", "label": "scripts/ research tooling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L44-L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately not part of the test suite - most need network, some need hours - but they are how each measured result is reproduced rather than taken on trust."}, {"id": "docs_development_compare_pooling", "label": "scripts/compare_pooling.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scores a pooled model on each symbol's own validation slice separately, which train()'s aggregated metric cannot do. Reported in investigations.md#pyq-315."}, {"id": "docs_development_ablate_features", "label": "scripts/ablate_features.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Walk-forward backtests across cumulative feature groups plus a correlation matrix naming the redundant technicals. Reported in investigations.md#pyq-316 and bugs.md#pyq-140."}, {"id": "docs_development_profile_forecast", "label": "scripts/profile_forecast.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Times a cold and a warm forecast call split into bundle-load / fetch+panel-build / predict. Reported in investigations.md#pyq-319 and the API design note."}, {"id": "docs_development_runs_py", "label": "scripts/runs.py compare", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L55-L62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads every bundle's runs.jsonl and lines the fields up. It is also an argument in itself: the ~100-line alternative shipped instead of taking on mlflow as a dependency."}, {"id": "docs_development_record_fixtures", "label": "scripts/record_fixtures.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Refreshes the checked-in vendor payloads the contract tests read; article text is replaced with placeholders because the tests care about response shape, not copyrighted copy."}, {"id": "docs_development_backlog_script", "label": "scripts/backlog.py check|list", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backlog consistency and priority-sorted open tickets; no dependencies, runs from a bare clone."}, {"id": "docs_development_dependency_justification", "label": "New dependencies need a recorded reason", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L59-L62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mypy in CI and a real-FinBERT CI job were both declined on measured evidence, and that disposition is a feature."}, {"id": "docs_development_backlog", "label": "backlog/ as source of truth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L64-L84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "IDs never move between files and tickets never move within a file - only the Status line changes - which is what makes 'see PYQ-109' a permanent link. Enforced by backlog.py check, not stylistic."}, {"id": "docs_development_resolution_note", "label": "Resolution note standard", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L76-L84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not a changelog entry: it states behaviour change, the decision made, verification evidence with real before/after numbers, the guarding tests, and what the fix invalidates elsewhere. These notes are why the docs can cite a ticket instead of restating an argument."}, {"id": "docs_development_docs_build", "label": "Building the docs site", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L86-L106", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "--extra api is required, not optional: pyquant/api/ imports fastapi at module level, autodoc imports every module it documents, and fail_on_warning would fail the whole build over one section most readers never open. Colour tokens live in conf.py theme options and structure in _static/custom.css so a value is defined once per theme."}, {"id": "docs_development_warnings_as_errors", "label": "Docs built with -W --keep-going", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L94-L99", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A docs site not built with warnings-as-errors rots within two refactors: a renamed module, a dead :func: reference or an autodoc import failure all degrade silently otherwise. A nightly job re-resolves intersphinx inventories so an upstream removal is caught by a scheduled run rather than by a reader."}, {"id": "docs_development_metric_honesty", "label": "Never make a metric look better without making the model better", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L110-L114", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The project's credibility rests on having replaced 'directional accuracy 100.0%' with an honest '57.5% on 280 points'. If a past number turns out wrong, say so loudly and supersede the tickets that relied on it."}, {"id": "docs_development_lookahead_leakage", "label": "Look-ahead leakage is the top risk", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L116-L120", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every leak found so far was correct in each individual file and wrong across files. Before any change to data/ or split geometry ask whether a row at time t can now see information that did not exist at time t; twice, 'what does decoder_time_idx actually contain' was the entire bug."}, {"id": "docs_development_measured_not_expected", "label": "Every claim must be measured, not expected", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L122-L124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rationale for why something should help is not a result. Pooling was described that way once; it is now a measured - and corrected - claim."}, {"id": "docs_development_comments_cite_tickets", "label": "Comments explain why and cite ticket IDs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L126-L128", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The convention is how the code and the backlog stay connected; there are dozens of such references across pyquant/."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_development_profile_forecast", "target": "docs_api_design_latency_profile", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L54", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_compare_pooling", "target": "docs_cli_pooling_not_free_win", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L52", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_ablate_features", "target": "docs_cli_train", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L53", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_research_scripts", "target": "docs_development_compare_pooling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L50-L57", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_research_scripts", "target": "docs_development_ablate_features", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L50-L57", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_research_scripts", "target": "docs_development_profile_forecast", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L50-L57", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_research_scripts", "target": "docs_development_runs_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/development.md", "source_location": "L50-L57", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_development_research_scripts", "target